rd"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphOperations\/documentation\/GraphOperations\/SubgraphView","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"SubgraphView","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SubgraphView","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A subgraph of a graph, as a lazy view: some of its vertices and some of its edges, renumbered"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"densely. Made by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inducedSubgraphView(on:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spanningSubgraphView(edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"subgraphView(vertices:edges:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphoperations\/subgraphview"},"doc://Connectivity/documentation/Connectivity/KComponents":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"KComponents"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Connectivity\/documentation\/Connectivity\/KComponents","kind":"symbol","title":"KComponents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The k-components of an undirected graph (Moody and White’s cohesive blocking): for each k ≥ 1,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the maximal sets of vertices whose induced subgraph is k-vertex-connected, that is, has more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than k vertices and stays connected after removing any k − 1 of them. The 1-components are the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"connected components with an edge, the 2-components the blocks of three or more vertices; every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"k-component lies inside a (k − 1)-component. Components at one level may share fewer than k"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices."}],"url":"\/documentation\/connectivity\/kcomponents","type":"topic","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"